sjdevnull@yahoo.com wrote:
>
> Also bear in mind that although it's possible, it's not always worth
> it.
>
> Blessed, greased, +7 elven boots give you 8 AC and stealth.
> Blessed, greased, very corroded +7 elven boots give you 7 AC and
> stealth.

I thought elven boots rot or burn not corrode or rust.  It does not
matter because they are really just named based on the exact same bits
in the data structures.

> Worrying about rust and corrosion is one of the very, very last things
> you should even consider, and most middling to reasonably experienced
> players ignore it entirely unless they happen to find many more
> scrolls of enchant armor than they need.

One reason is it's tempting to waste the scrolls on your early non-kit
armor.  If you're targetting teeshirt, GDSM, robe, speed, dexterity,
brilliance and "oR then it's not worth proofing other types of armor no
matter how enchanted it is.  Unless you've got the scrolls to spare.

> Honestly, rust/corrosion just aren't a big deal.

Weapons have already been mentioned.  By the mid-game I might have a few
long swords but by then I've likely got a proofed artifact as my main
melee weapon.  If I use a saber as my alternate/dual wield proofing has
no effect.  I've proofed big stacks of elven daggers but they don't see
much damage when thrown.  Damage matters with weapons but the weapons
themselves end up disposible.


